WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.120
- So, your husband though,
he just - Chris Pratt -

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.547
he had a birthday,
right, a recent birthday?

00:00:03.547 --> 00:00:05.360
- Oh yeah, last - last June.
- [Kelly] What'd you get him?

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.010
- I got him piggies.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.490
- [Kelly] You got him actual pigs.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:09.330
- Yeah, I did.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.397
- What, like miniature ones?

00:00:10.397 --> 00:00:11.410
- No.
- No.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.870
- Well, actually what happened to me

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:13.730
when I was in high school

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.560
was I rescued this supposed miniature pig

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.393
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:00:17.393 --> 00:00:19.660
- When I lived at my
parents' house (laughs).

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.260
And it turned into a giant pot-bellied pig

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.572
and rooted up my mom's entire lawn

00:00:24.572 --> 00:00:26.010
- (laughs) I'm just laughing because of-

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.450
nobody's actually had a huge
pot-bellied - they're enormous.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.440
- They're so big, very, very large.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.310
Yeah, that's Bacon, my pig.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.613
She's since passed away.

00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:34.610
- (laughs) You named her Bacon.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.443
- I know.

00:00:35.443 --> 00:00:37.700
My little brother Christopher
actually named her Bacon,

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.820
so it's his fault.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.160
But yeah, he has...

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.410
We have an amazing place
in Washington State,

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.460
so there's a lot of land there,

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.130
so the pig - these pigs
are not living with us.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.014
- They're living in a very beautiful farm,

00:00:47.014 --> 00:00:49.130
- [Kelly] On a farm, yeah!

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.960
- Loving life, very large now,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.180
so I'm very excited that they
did not come to our house

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.720
because I was told they would stay small.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.660
They did not.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.980
- Yeah, I was told my dog
was gonna be miniature

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.631
and lies and deception!

00:00:59.631 --> 00:01:00.860
- (laughs)

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.420
- Heifer's like forty-five pounds.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.287
I'm like, "What?

00:01:03.287 --> 00:01:04.880
"He is not fifteen to eighteen pounds."

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:05.713
- I know.

00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:07.000
- That's awesomeness, y'all
have a farm in Washington?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.150
Washington's beautiful.
- Yeah.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.250
- Yeah.
- Yeah, it's beautiful.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.640
- Nice place to escape, that's cool.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.470
- Yeah. Yeah, I grew up around animals,

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:13.440
so it's really fun and--

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.310
- [Kelly] I did as well. Yeah.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.770
- I love it, it makes me so happy.

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:16.620
- Animals are so cool.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.570
They're just loyal and nice,

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.298
and they're never mean.

00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:22.077
- (laughs) So have y'all
ever had any unusual pets?

00:01:22.077 --> 00:01:23.730
- I used to have this babysitter,

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.150
and she had a rooster.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.020
- Oh, they can be mean.
- [Katherine] Yeah, and loud.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.820
- That's the thing.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:30.783
It was very mean.

00:01:30.783 --> 00:01:32.360
Because she would go outside

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.410
and she loved the rooster,

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:34.243
because how could you

00:01:34.243 --> 00:01:35.076
not love animals?

00:01:35.076 --> 00:01:37.067
- And she would go outside--
- [Kelly] I don't

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:37.900
love roosters.
- and try to bond with it,

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.298
and it would try to bite her.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:42.360
And at a certain point it was chasing her

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.230
all around the yard and
she climbed up a tree

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.767
and it bit her butt. And it was horrible.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:46.640
(audience laughs)

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.210
- Oh my God, that happened to me one time

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.043
in a little petting zoo.

00:01:49.043 --> 00:01:50.300
My sister, I was holding her child

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.960
and this goat kept nippin' at my behind.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.558
I was like, "Get your child off of me!"

00:01:53.558 --> 00:01:56.210
'Cause I was holding
her kid, from the goat

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.700
and my sister's just laughing.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.263
I'm like, "It's eating my butt!"

00:01:59.263 --> 00:02:00.640
I was like, "Quit!"

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.473
Anyway.

